# Keep the checksum sidecar byte-identical on every platform.
# Git's autocrlf would otherwise hand Windows a CRLF copy, which the build
# rewrites with LF on the next run — a phantom "modified file" after every
# fresh clone. Pinning it to LF makes the file the same everywhere.
*.sha256 text eol=lf

# The published download must never be touched by Git. It is the file whose
# SHA-256 we advertise, so any end-of-line conversion would silently break
# checksum verification for everyone who downloads it. Git detects binary
# on its own, but this is too important to leave to detection.
*.zip  binary
*.png  binary
*.webp binary
*.ico  binary
